      "message": "Take only so many strangers, and only reachable ones\n\nWith --open-signup a stranger had the whole free tier the moment\nthey typed a name: no cap on accounts, so accounts times the disk\nquota was unbounded, and nothing was gated on an address anybody\ncould reach them at. The forge now knows who made their own account\n(principals gains self_made, projected from the registration being\nthe person's own; schema 31, rehearsed on a copy of the flagship),\nand such an account creates nothing — no repository, no agent —\nuntil an address of theirs is confirmed. --signup-cap says how many\nself-made accounts the forge takes; past it the page says the forge\nis full, and the form is not a way around the page. A forge opened\nwithout --trust-proxy warns at start that every stranger behind the\nproxy shares one sign-up allowance.\n\nChange-Id: Isignupcap0116\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
